      "reason": "Nitracline should be derived from each model's native vertical profiles, then regridded only for maps and pattern comparison to WOA23, since regridding changes masks and is not conservative.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute global and basin mean nitracline depths on each source's own grid with its own `areacello`; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the maps, the pattern correlation and the RMSE, and state the method ('conservative' when coarsening).",
        "The nitracline is a vertical-extremum diagnostic quantised by each source's vertical grid, so read the maps alongside the gradient and note that the depth resolution differs between products."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 nitrate is stored per volume (mol m-3) while WOA23 is per mass, so the fields must be converted to one unit before gradients, depths or RMSE are computed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `no3` is mol m-3 and WOA23 is µmol kg-1, so Figure 2's single shared concentration unit and any absolute comparison require a conversion using in-situ density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`), stating `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "The nitracline depth (depth of a maximum gradient) is scale-invariant: a constant ρ cancels, while the depth-varying in-situ density would shift it slightly — locate the depth on the native basis and say so."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "GFDL-ESM4 nitrate is already conservatively regridded (gr), while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native (gn), which affects masks and exact operations.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its values, land-sea mask and `volcello` are already remapped (conserve_order1, 75→35 z levels), so its \"native-grid\" numbers are archive-grid numbers and its budgets only approximately conservative.",
        "Resolution differs by ~2.5× (CESM2 100 km, MPI 250 km), so narrow features are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and basin nitracline means must be area-weighted with areacello over all valid ocean cells, not simple grid-point averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Every global and basin nitracline mean is area-weighted: `compute_basic_stat(op='area_weighted_mean')` with `areacello` masked to the same valid cells; unweighted means on a curvilinear grid are wrong.",
        "The map-to-map Pearson correlation needs `analyze_correlation(weighting='area')`; `compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default."
      ]
    },
    {
