      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "Nitracline depth is a nonlinear diagnostic of monthly mean nitrate, so deriving it from climatological monthly means differs from averaging monthly nitracline depths and must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The nitracline is nonlinear in nitrate, so state the order: average first, then locate the maximum gradient, is the like-for-like choice against the WOA23 climatology (diagnostic-first would give the time mean of monthly nitraclines).",
        "Build the models' 1971-2000 mean with `temporal_aggregate(freq='mean')` so months carry calendar-length weights; `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights every month equally."
      ]
    },
